# Styling Standards

## Typography

- **Apostrophes**: ALL user-facing text MUST use the typographic apostrophe ’ instead of the straight apostrophe '
- **Consistency**: Maintain consistent typography throughout the application

## Tailwind CSS

- **Custom utilities**: Use or extend utilities from `src/index.css` (e.g. `.grid-cols-16`) when needed
- **Theme color utilities**: Use the project’s defined color tokens for all UI colors — do not hardcode hex/rgb/oklch in components, reach for raw Tailwind palette names (`stone-*`, `cyan-*`, etc.), or apply opacity modifiers to color utilities (no `bg-light/60`, `bg-dark/50`, etc.)
- **Shared surface classes**: Prefer the reusable `*ClassName` constants in `src/lib/control-classes.ts` for repeated background/foreground pairings
- **Direct strings**: Use direct strings for simple cases without conditionals
- **No margins**: Avoid using Tailwind margin classes (`m-*`, `mx-*`, `my-*`, `mt-*`, `mr-*`, `mb-*`, `ml-*`)
- **No space utilities**: Avoid `space-x-*` or `space-y-*` utilities — they rely on margins
- **Formatting**: Use Biome for formatting and linting (including class order where applicable)
- **Utility function**: Use `clsx()` for conditional classes (not `cn()`)

### Color & Theme

Theme tokens are defined in `src/index.css` (`@theme`) and exposed as Tailwind utilities. They use `light-dark()` so light/dark/system mode stays consistent when `data-theme` changes.

**Semantic tokens** (prefer these):

| Token | Typical use |
|-------|-------------|
| `white` / `black` | Page and modal surfaces; invert between modes |
| `surface` / `surface-muted` | Inset panels, measure cells, secondary controls |
| `dark` / `light` / `mid` | Borders, settings panels, muted body text |
| `scrim` | Modal backdrop overlay |
| `primary` / `secondary` | Accents, active states, playback highlights |
| `chrome` / `chrome-hover` | Header/footer controls, popovers, icon buttons |

If a color needs translucency, define it in `@theme` (e.g. `--color-scrim`) — do not use Tailwind’s `/opacity` suffix on color utilities in components.

**Shared surface helpers** (`src/lib/control-classes.ts`):

| Constant | Use for |
|----------|---------|
| `pageSurfaceClassName` | App shell (`bg-white text-black`) |
| `darkSurfaceClassName` | Sections, empty prompts (`bg-surface text-black`) |
| `modalScrimClassName` / `modalPanelClassName` | Modal overlay (`bg-scrim`) and dialog panel |
| `settingsPanelClassName` | Settings grouping panels (`bg-light text-dark`) |
| `inputSurfaceClassName` | Text/number inputs on themed backgrounds |
| `controlButtonBaseClassName` | Chrome icon/action buttons (`bg-chrome text-black`) |
| `controlSurfaceBaseClassName` | Bordered chrome panels (ShowNotes popover, metronome bar) |

**Pair foreground with background**:

- Inset surfaces (`darkSurfaceClassName`, `bg-surface`): `text-black`
- Muted interactive surfaces (`bg-surface-muted`): `text-black`
- Chrome controls (`bg-chrome`, `controlButtonBaseClassName`): `text-black`
- Page/modal surfaces (`pageSurfaceClassName`, `modalPanelClassName`): `text-black`
- Settings-style panels (`settingsPanelClassName`, `bg-light`): `text-dark`
- Primary/accent controls (`bg-primary`): `text-white`
- Muted captions: `text-mid`
- Borders and hovers: `border-mid`, `hover:border-primary`, `hover:bg-mid` or `hover:bg-chrome-hover`

```tsx
import clsx from 'clsx';
import {
	darkSurfaceClassName,
	modalPanelClassName,
	pageSurfaceClassName,
} from '@/lib/control-classes';

// Page shell
className={clsx('App flex min-h-dvh flex-col', pageSurfaceClassName)}

// Section panel
className={clsx('Section flex flex-col gap-4 border border-mid rounded-lg p-4', darkSurfaceClassName)}

// Modal dialog panel
className={clsx('relative flex flex-col gap-4 p-6', modalPanelClassName)}

// One-off accent control — still use theme tokens inline
className='border border-mid bg-primary text-white hover:border-white'
```

Do **not** rely on inherited page text color inside dark panels or modals rendered outside the App shell — set the appropriate surface helper or explicit `text-*` token on the container.

### ClassName Patterns

```tsx
// Component name should be first in className for debugging
className={clsx('ComponentName rounded-lg border border-mid p-4', darkSurfaceClassName)}

// Conditional cases - use clsx
className={clsx(
  'ComponentName base-classes',
  isActive && 'active-classes',
  isDisabled && 'disabled-classes',
)}

// Component variants - use a variant prop, not className passthrough
type ComponentProps = {
  variant?: 'default' | 'title';
};

className={clsx(
  'ComponentName base-classes',
  variant === 'title' && 'title-classes',
)}
```

- **No `className` props on components**: Do not accept `className` on shared components for styling customization. Encode supported visual differences as a `variant` prop (see `ControlButton`, `AboutPoisonRhythmButton`).

### JSX Attribute Order

Follow this specific order for JSX attributes:

1. **type** - Element type (for form elements)
2. **className** - CSS classes
3. **Standard HTML attributes** - (alphabetically)
4. **Event handlers** - (alphabetically, starting with 'on')
5. **ARIA attributes** - (alphabetically)
6. **Custom data attributes** - (alphabetically)
7. **ref** - React ref (penultimate)
8. **id** - Element identifier (always last)

#### JSX Attribute Order Example

```tsx
<button
	type='button'
	className={clsx(
		'Button rounded-lg border border-mid p-4',
		darkSurfaceClassName,
	)}
	disabled={isDisabled}
	title='Submit form'
	onClick={handleClick}
	onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
	aria-label='Submit form'
	aria-describedby='submit-help'
	data-testid='submit-button'
	ref={buttonRef}
	id='submit-button'
>
	Submit
</button>
```

### Layout Principles

- **Flexbox/Grid**: Use Flexbox and Grid for layouts
- **Avoid margins**: Don't use CSS margins except for printing and where flex/grid won't work
- **Avoid space- utilities**: Don't use `space-x-*` or `space-y-*` — they rely on margins
- **Use flex/gap**: Use `flex flex-col gap-*` for vertical spacing and `flex items-center gap-*` for horizontal spacing
- **Consistent spacing**: Use Tailwind's spacing scale

### Spacing Patterns

```tsx
// Vertical spacing
className='flex flex-col gap-2';   // Small gaps
className='flex flex-col gap-4';   // Medium gaps
className='flex flex-col gap-6';   // Large gaps

// Horizontal spacing
className='flex items-center gap-2';
className='flex justify-between';

// Responsive spacing
className='flex flex-col gap-3 sm:gap-4';
className='flex items-center gap-1.5 sm:gap-2';
```

### Component Structure

- **Avoid superfluous wrappers**: Don't create unnecessary wrapper divs that add DOM complexity
- **Simplify nesting**: Remove redundant wrapper elements when possible
- **Keep meaningful wrappers**: Retain wrappers that serve styling, semantic, or organizational purposes

#### Wrapper Removal Examples

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid - redundant wrapper
<div className='flex flex-col gap-6'>
  <div className='flex flex-col gap-6'>
    <Component />
  </div>
</div>

// ✅ Good - simplified structure
<div className='flex flex-col gap-6'>
  <Component />
</div>
```

## CSS Best Practices

- **Theme colors only**: Define palette values in `src/index.css` `@theme`; consume them via Tailwind utilities or `control-classes.ts` helpers in components
- **No !important**: Avoid using `!important` declarations in CSS
- **TypeScript**: Avoid using the `any` type in TypeScript code
- **Semantic HTML**: Use semantic HTML elements for better accessibility
